// P6 `dl` (CONTRACT-P6 5.2, D2 ruling). THE INTERNAL FATAL VOCABULARY, and its projection onto
// the SEVEN-value wire FatalCode.
//
// a6 censused 30 distinct family words against a 7-value wire enum, so Session::Fail(FatalCode,
// detail) cannot carry the vocabulary in its first argument - the word would collapse to one of
// seven and the log would say "ProtocolCorruption" where the code said "UnmigratedVerb". So the
// family is an INTERNAL enum, generated from this file, and the wire keeps FatalCode. Each row
// carries the coarse code the PEER is told when this family kills the session; the rich word
// stays in the local log and in the SessionFault frame's `family` string.
//
// THE PROJECTION IS A TOTAL TABLE, NOT A SWITCH WITH A DEFAULT. This build has no -Werror
// anywhere (measured: CMakeLists, every *.cmake, both workflows), so a gate premised on -Wswitch
// catching a missing arm is fiction. A row here IS the arm; a family with no row does not
// compile a call that names it.
//
// WHY EACH CODE. The wire FatalCode answers one question for the peer: what KIND of end was
// this. The buckets:
//   ProtocolCorruption - the peer sent, or the session reached, something that cannot be
//                        honoured correctly: a malformed record, an unimplemented verb/surface,
//                        an invariant the roles must hold, a reply that does not fit its
//                        contract. The peer's takeaway is "we disagree about the protocol".
//   RingOverrun        - a shared ring or event channel overran. A transport-capacity fact.
//   SegmentMismatch    - a shared SEGMENT's geometry could not hold what a role needed to put
//                        in it. Distinct from a ring overrun: the segment is the wrong SIZE,
//                        not merely full this instant.
//   AbiMismatch        - the two builds do not agree on layout or protocol version.
//   ServerCrashed      - a liveness end the WAITING side attributes to the other: a drain that
//                        never completed, an apply thread that is gone or never started. The
//                        device-lost latch is armed from the doorbell, never from these, but the
//                        peer that was waiting is told the server is gone.
//   DeviceLost         - reserved: set by the latch (5.3), never raised as a Fatal family, so no
//                        row projects onto it.
//
// clang-format off

// X(Family, WireFatalCode, Why)
#define MGL_FATAL_FAMILY_LIST(X) \
    X(ProtocolCorruption,            ProtocolCorruption, "a record's bounds or self-describing length was violated") \
    X(UnmigratedVerb,                ProtocolCorruption, "a wire verb slot P5/P6 does not implement was reached") \
    X(UnmigratedSurface,             ProtocolCorruption, "a surface op named a client-process handle that means nothing here (P12)") \
    X(UnmigratedPipeInput,           ProtocolCorruption, "a PipeInputs field with no field-ownership row was read across the boundary") \
    X(RoleViolation,                 ProtocolCorruption, "a call ran on the wrong role/thread - an invariant the two roles must hold") \
    X(UnsetCallMask,                 ProtocolCorruption, "the CallMask was consulted before either half was published") \
    X(ClientTablesUninstalled,       ProtocolCorruption, "the applier ran before the client installed its tables") \
    X(NoClientSession,               ProtocolCorruption, "a path that needs the client session ran without one") \
    X(UnexpectedMapAccept,           ProtocolCorruption, "a persistent-map accept arrived where the protocol permits none") \
    X(UncarriedInitialBytes,         ProtocolCorruption, "a producer's initial bytes were required on the wire and absent") \
    X(ReplyStatusInvalid,            ProtocolCorruption, "a reply carried a status outside the defined set") \
    X(ReplyError,                    ProtocolCorruption, "a reply-owning verb saw an error status it cannot represent") \
    X(ReplyMissing,                  ProtocolCorruption, "a reply slot the protocol requires was empty") \
    X(ReplyTooLarge,                 ProtocolCorruption, "an answer exceeded the size its verb's contract allows") \
    X(ReadbackDeclined,              ProtocolCorruption, "a readback that cannot return without complete pixels was declined") \
    X(ReadbackReplyShort,            ProtocolCorruption, "a readback reply carried fewer bytes than its shape requires") \
    X(UnsizedReadback,               ProtocolCorruption, "a readback arrived with no declared size") \
    X(BlobMissing,                   ProtocolCorruption, "a record named a blob that was never staged") \
    X(BlobNotStaged,                 ProtocolCorruption, "a blob was referenced before its staging completed") \
    X(ArtefactsMissing,              ProtocolCorruption, "a program create arrived with no artefacts") \
    X(ArchiveEmpty,                  ProtocolCorruption, "a create_*_state archive carried no payload") \
    X(BarrierViolation,             ProtocolCorruption, "a field was pulled across a verb boundary the barrier forbids") \
    X(UnimplementedAdoptTier,        ProtocolCorruption, "MOBILEGL_IPC_ADOPT_TIER named a tier P5 does not implement") \
    X(UnimplementedWritebackWait,    ProtocolCorruption, "a writeback wait shape P5 does not implement was requested") \
    X(UnimplementedRemoteBackendObject, ProtocolCorruption, "a BackendObject_Remote entry point P5 does not implement was called") \
    X(UnimplementedClientSession,    ProtocolCorruption, "a ClientSession entry point P5 does not implement was called") \
    X(RingOverrun,                   RingOverrun,        "a shared ring refused a record after sufficient space had retired") \
    X(EventRingOverflow,             RingOverrun,        "the reverse event ring overflowed") \
    X(StageSnapshotTooNarrow,        SegmentMismatch,    "SEG_STAGE was too small for a snapshot a verb had to place in it") \
    X(AbiMismatch,                   AbiMismatch,        "the two builds disagree on struct layout or protocol version") \
    X(BarrierTimeout,                ServerCrashed,      "appliedSeq did not reach the target within the bounded wait") \
    X(PresentCreditTimeout,          ServerCrashed,      "a present credit did not return within the bounded wait") \
    X(RetirementWaitFailed,          ServerCrashed,      "a wait for the server to retire staging did not complete") \
    X(ApplyThreadJoinTimeout,        ServerCrashed,      "the apply thread did not join within its bound at teardown") \
    X(ApplyThreadNotRunning,         ServerCrashed,      "an operation needed the apply thread and it was not running")

// clang-format on
